    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "In this Act:\nAboriginal person has the same meaning as in the Aboriginal and\nTorres Strait Islander Act 2005.\nAdvisory Council means the Advisory Council of the Australian\nCentre for Disease Control established by section 26.\nAdvisory Council member: see subsection 28(1).\nAgriculture Department means the Department administered by\nthe Agriculture Minister.\nAgriculture Minister means the Minister administering the\nPrimary Industries Levies and Charges Collection Act 2024.\nappointed member means an Advisory Council member appointed\nby the Minister under subsection 30(1).\nAustralian government entity means:\n(a) a Commonwealth entity; or\n(b) a State or Territory government entity.\nCentre means the Australian Centre for Disease Control\nestablished by section 7.\ncivil penalty provision has the same meaning as in the Regulatory\nPowers Act.\nCommonwealth entity has the same meaning as in the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013.\ndata service has the same meaning as in the Data Availability and\nTransparency Act 2022.\ndata sharing declaration means a declaration made under\nsubsection 67(1).\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 5\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\ndesignated data service provider: see section 42.\ndesignated secrecy law means the following:\n(a) the Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism\nFinancing Act 2006;\n(b) the Australian Crime Commission Act 2002;\n(c) the Australian Federal Police Act 1979;\n(d) the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979;\n(e) the Defence Act 1903;\n(f) the Intelligence Services Act 2001;\n(g) the National Security Information (Criminal and Civil\nProceedings) Act 2004;\n(h) the Office of National Intelligence Act 2018;\n(i) any other law, or provision of a law, of the Commonwealth, a\nState or a Territory that is prescribed by the rules.\nDirector-General means the Director-General of the Australian\nCentre for Disease Control appointed by the Minister under\nsection 10.\ndisability has the same meaning as in the Disability Discrimination\nAct 1992.\nenactment means:\n(a) an Act of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; or\n(b) an instrument (including rules, regulations and by-laws)\nmade under an Act of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory.\nentrusted person means any of the following:\n(a) the Minister;\n(b) the Director-General;\n(c) any other Advisory Council member;\n(d) an APS employee in the Centre;\n(e) a member of an advisory board established by the\nDirector-General under subsection 24(1) of the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013;\n(f) an APS employee in the Department;",
      "skos:definition": "In this Act:\nAboriginal person has the same meaning as in the Aboriginal and\nTorres Strait Islander Act 2005.\nAdvisory Council means the Advisory Council of the Australian\nCentre for Disease Control established by section 26.\nAdvisory Council member: see subsection 28(1).\nAgriculture Department means the Department administered by\nthe Agriculture Minister.\nAgriculture Minister means the Minister administering the\nPrimary Industries Levies and Charges Collection Act 2024.\nappointed member means an Advisory Council member appointed\nby the Minister under subsection 30(1).\nAustralian government entity means:\n(a) a Commonwealth entity; or\n(b) a State or Territory government entity.\nCentre means the Australian Centre for Disease Control\nestablished by section 7.\ncivil penalty provision has the same meaning as in the Regulatory\nPowers Act.\nCommonwealth entity has the same meaning as in the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013.\ndata service has the same meaning as in the Data Availability and\nTransparency Act 2022.\ndata sharing declaration means a declaration made under\nsubsection 67(1).\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 5\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\ndesignated data service provider: see section 42.\ndesignated secrecy law means the following:\n(a) the Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism\nFinancing Act 2006;\n(b) the Australian Crime Commission Act 2002;\n(c) the Australian Federal Police Act 1979;\n(d) the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979;\n(e) the Defence Act 1903;\n(f) the Intelligence Services Act 2001;\n(g) the National Security Information (Criminal and Civil\nProceedings) Act 2004;\n(h) the Office of National Intelligence Act 2018;\n(i) any other law, or provision of a law, of the Commonwealth, a\nState or a Territory that is prescribed by the rules.\nDirector-General means the Director-General of the Australian\nCentre for Disease Control appointed by the Minister under\nsection 10.\ndisability has the ",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-5-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-5-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e218abbc606ce95533b0ee316a3ce30eff9fbab5c514055059bdd7012d272b9d",
      "skos:note": "Definitions for the Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "In this Act:\nAboriginal person has the same meaning as in the Aboriginal and\nTorres Strait Islander Act 2005.\nAdvisory Council means the Advisory Council of the Australian\nCentre for Disease Control established by section 26.\nAdvisory Council member: see subsection 28(1).\nAgriculture Department means the Department administered by\nthe Agriculture Minister.\nAgriculture Minister means the Minister administering the\nPrimary Industries Levies and Charges Collection Act 2024.\nappointed member means an Advisory Council member appointed\nby the Minister under subsection 30(1).\nAustralian government entity means:\n(a) a Commonwealth entity; or\n(b) a State or Territory government entity.\nCentre means the Australian Centre for Disease Control\nestablished by section 7.\ncivil penalty provision has the same meaning as in the Regulatory\nPowers Act.\nCommonwealth entity has the same meaning as in the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013.\ndata service has the same meaning as in the Data Availability and\nTransparency Act 2022.\ndata sharing declaration means a declaration made under\nsubsection 67(1).\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 5\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\ndesignated data service provider: see section 42.\ndesignated secrecy law means the following:\n(a) the Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism\nFinancing Act 2006;\n(b) the Australian Crime Commission Act 2002;\n(c) the Australian Federal Police Act 1979;\n(d) the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979;\n(e) the Defence Act 1903;\n(f) the Intelligence Services Act 2001;\n(g) the National Security Information (Criminal and Civil\nProceedings) Act 2004;\n(h) the Office of National Intelligence Act 2018;\n(i) any other law, or provision of a law, of the Commonwealth, a\nState or a Territory that is prescribed by the rules.\nDirector-General means the Director-General of the Australian\nCentre for Disease Control appointed by the Minister under\nsection 10.\ndisability has the same meaning as in the Disability Discrimination\nAct 1992.\nenactment means:\n(a) an Act of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; or\n(b) an instrument (including rules, regulations and by-laws)\nmade under an Act of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory.\nentrusted person means any of the following:\n(a) the Minister;\n(b) the Director-General;\n(c) any other Advisory Council member;\n(d) an APS employee in the Centre;\n(e) a member of an advisory board established by the\nDirector-General under subsection 24(1) of the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013;\n(f) an APS employee in the Department;"
    },
