      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Director-General holds office for a period of 5 years unless a\nshorter period is specified in the instrument of appointment.\nNote:\nThe Director-General may be reappointed: see section 33AA of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The Director-General holds office for a period of 5 years unless a\nshorter period is specified in the instrument of appointment.\nNote:\nThe Director-General may be reappointed: see section 33AA of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901.",
