    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-13",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13 Powers of the Director-General",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-13"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "Necessary or convenient power\n(1) The Director-General has power to do all things necessary or\nconvenient to be done for, or in connection with, the performance\nof the Director-General’s functions and duties.\nEntering into agreements\n(2) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), the\nDirector-General may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, enter into\nan agreement with any of the following if the agreement relates to\nthe functions, duties or powers of the Director-General or the\nCentre:\n(a) a State;\n(b) a Territory;\n(c) a State or Territory government entity.\nEntering into arrangements\n(3) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), the\nDirector-General may, on behalf of the Centre, enter into an\narrangement with any of the following if the arrangement relates to\nthe functions, duties or powers of the Director-General or the\nCentre:\n(a) a foreign government body;\n(b) an international organisation;\n(c) an international partnership.\n\n\nThe Australian Centre for Disease Control  Part 2\nThe Director-General of the Australian Centre for Disease Control  Division 3\nSection 14\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025",
      "skos:definition": "Necessary or convenient power\n(1) The Director-General has power to do all things necessary or\nconvenient to be done for, or in connection with, the performance\nof the Director-General’s functions and duties.\nEntering into agreements\n(2) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), the\nDirector-General may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, enter into\nan agreement with any of the following if the agreement relates to\nthe functions, duties or powers of the Director-General or the\nCentre:\n(a) a State;\n(b) a Territory;\n(c) a State or Territory government entity.\nEntering into arrangements\n(3) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), the\nDirector-General may, on behalf of the Centre, enter into an\narrangement with any of the following if the arrangement relates to\nthe functions, duties or powers of the Director-General or the\nCentre:\n(a) a foreign government body;\n(b) an international organisation;\n(c) an international partnership.\n\n\nThe Australian Centre for Disease Control  Part 2\nThe Director-General of the Australian Centre for Disease Control  Division 3\nSection 14\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-13-ss-1"
        },
