    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-15",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15 Remuneration and conditions of appointment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-15"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "Remuneration and allowances\n(1) The Director-General is to be paid the remuneration that is\ndetermined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If no determination of\nthat remuneration by the Tribunal is in operation, the\nDirector-General is to be paid the remuneration that is prescribed\nin the rules for the purposes of this subsection.\n(2) The Director-General is to be paid the allowances that are\nprescribed in the rules.\nLeave of absence\n(3) The Director-General has the recreation leave entitlements that are\ndetermined by the Remuneration Tribunal.\n(4) The Minister may grant the Director-General leave of absence,\nother than recreation leave, on the terms and conditions as to\nremuneration or otherwise that the Minister determines.\n(5) This section has effect subject to the Remuneration Tribunal Act\n1973.",
      "skos:definition": "Remuneration and allowances\n(1) The Director-General is to be paid the remuneration that is\ndetermined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If no determination of\nthat remuneration by the Tribunal is in operation, the\nDirector-General is to be paid the remuneration that is prescribed\nin the rules for the purposes of this subsection.\n(2) The Director-General is to be paid the allowances that are\nprescribed in the rules.\nLeave of absence\n(3) The Director-General has the recreation leave entitlements that are\ndetermined by the Remuneration Tribunal.\n(4) The Minister may grant the Director-General leave of absence,\nother than recreation leave, on the terms and conditions as to\nremuneration or otherwise that the Minister determines.\n(5) This section has effect subject to the Remuneration Tribunal Act\n1973.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-15-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-15-ss-2"
        },
