    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-17",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "17 Termination of appointment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-17"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may terminate the appointment of the\nDirector-General:\n(a) for misbehaviour; or\n(b) if the Director-General is unable to perform the duties of the\nDirector-General’s office because of physical or mental\nincapacity.\n(2) The Minister may terminate the appointment of the\nDirector-General if:\n(a) the Director-General:\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n(ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n\n\nThe Australian Centre for Disease Control  Part 2\nThe Director-General of the Australian Centre for Disease Control  Division 3\nSection 17\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\n(iii) compounds with the Director-General’s creditors; or\n(iv) makes an assignment of the Director-General’s\nremuneration for the benefit of the Director-General’s\ncreditors; or\n(b) the Director-General is absent, except on leave of absence,\nfor 14 consecutive days or for 28 days in any 12 months; or\n(c) the Director-General engages, except with the Minister’s\napproval, in paid work outside the duties of the\nDirector-General’s office (see subsection 15(6)).\nNote:\nThe appointment of the Director-General may also be terminated\nunder section 30 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013 (which deals with terminating the\nappointment of an accountable authority, or a member of an\naccountable authority, for contravening general duties of officials).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may terminate the appointment of the\nDirector-General:\n(a) for misbehaviour; or\n(b) if the Director-General is unable to perform the duties of the\nDirector-General’s office because of physical or mental\nincapacity.\n(2) The Minister may terminate the appointment of the\nDirector-General if:\n(a) the Director-General:\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n(ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n\n\nThe Australian Centre for Disease Control  Part 2\nThe Director-General of the Australian Centre for Disease Control  Division 3\nSection 17\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\n(iii) compounds with the Director-General’s creditors; or\n(iv) makes an assignment of the Director-General’s\nremuneration for the benefit of the Director-General’s\ncreditors; or\n(b) the Director-General is absent, except on leave of absence,\nfor 14 consecutive days or for 28 days in any 12 months; or\n(c) the Director-General engages, except with the Minister’s\napproval, in paid work outside the duties of the\nDirector-General’s office (see subsection 15(6)).\nNote:\nThe appointment of the Director-General may also be terminated\nunder section 30 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013 (which deals with terminating the\nappointment of an accountable authority, or a member of an\naccountable authority, for contravening general duties of officials).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-17-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-17-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "88bed7d99b374fe330a9904747256f91ffe206f07698583c28ab57af4e7efdbd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-17",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17 Termination of appointment",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may terminate the appointment of the\nDirector-General:\n(a) for misbehaviour; or\n(b) if the Director-General is unable to perform the duties of the\nDirector-General’s office because of physical or mental\nincapacity.\n(2) The Minister may terminate the appointment of the\nDirector-General if:\n(a) the Director-General:\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n(ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n\n\nThe Australian Centre for Disease Control  Part 2\nThe Director-General of the Australian Centre for Disease Control  Division 3\nSection 17\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\n(iii) compounds with the Director-General’s creditors; or\n(iv) makes an assignment of the Director-General’s\nremuneration for the benefit of the Director-General’s\ncreditors; or\n(b) the Director-General is absent, except on leave of absence,\nfor 14 consecutive days or for 28 days in any 12 months; or\n(c) the Director-General engages, except with the Minister’s\napproval, in paid work outside the duties of the\nDirector-General’s office (see subsection 15(6)).\nNote:\nThe appointment of the Director-General may also be terminated\nunder section 30 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013 (which deals with terminating the\nappointment of an accountable authority, or a member of an\naccountable authority, for contravening general duties of officials)."
    },
