    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-22",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "22 Public health advice that is exempt material",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-22"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General must not publish advice under section 21 if\nthe Director-General is satisfied that the advice is exempt material.\nNote:\nFor exempt material, see section 5.\n(2) However, if the Director-General is satisfied that:\n(a) the advice is exempt material; but\n(b) it is possible for the Director-General to prepare a copy of the\nadvice, modified by deletions, that would not be exempt\nmaterial;\nthe Director-General must:\n(c) prepare a modified copy of the advice as mentioned in\nparagraph (b); and\n(d) cause the modified copy to be published under section 21.\nAnnual report must include reasons for exemption\n(3) The annual report prepared by the Director-General and given to\nthe Minister under section 46 of the Public Governance,\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013 for a period must, for\nany advice that was not published, or was published in modified\nform, under section 21 because of this section during the period,\n\n\nThe Australian Centre for Disease Control  Part 2\nPublication of public health advice  Division 5\nSection 23\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\ninclude the reasons why the advice was not published, or was\npublished in modified form.\n(4) For the purposes of subsection (3), it is sufficient for the annual\nreport to specify the subparagraph or subparagraphs of\nparagraph (a) or (b) of the definition of exempt material in\nsection 5 of this Act that applied to the advice, or that paragraph (c)\nof that definition applied.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Director-General must not publish advice under section 21 if\nthe Director-General is satisfied that the advice is exempt material.\nNote:\nFor exempt material, see section 5.\n(2) However, if the Director-General is satisfied that:\n(a) the advice is exempt material; but\n(b) it is possible for the Director-General to prepare a copy of the\nadvice, modified by deletions, that would not be exempt\nmaterial;\nthe Director-General must:\n(c) prepare a modified copy of the advice as mentioned in\nparagraph (b); and\n(d) cause the modified copy to be published under section 21.\nAnnual report must include reasons for exemption\n(3) The annual report prepared by the Director-General and given to\nthe Minister under section 46 of the Public Governance,\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013 for a period must, for\nany advice that was not published, or was published in modified\nform, under section 21 because of this section during the period,\n\n\nThe Australian Centre for Disease Control  Part 2\nPublication of public health advice  Division 5\nSection 23\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\ninclude the reasons why the advice was not published, or was\npublished in modified form.\n(4) For the purposes of subsection (3), it is sufficient for the annual\nreport to specify the subparagraph or subparagraphs of\nparagraph (a) or (b) of the definition of exempt material in\nsection 5 of this Act that applied to the advice, or that paragraph (c)\nof that definition applied.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-22-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-22-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-22-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-22-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0dc4341db4b55eccaf9c2ffcdd5f8ed9e96190e1d391bedfd9180b713acdbe8a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-22",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22 Public health advice that is exempt material",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General must not publish advice under section 21 if\nthe Director-General is satisfied that the advice is exempt material.\nNote:\nFor exempt material, see section 5.\n(2) However, if the Director-General is satisfied that:\n(a) the advice is exempt material; but\n(b) it is possible for the Director-General to prepare a copy of the\nadvice, modified by deletions, that would not be exempt\nmaterial;\nthe Director-General must:\n(c) prepare a modified copy of the advice as mentioned in\nparagraph (b); and\n(d) cause the modified copy to be published under section 21.\nAnnual report must include reasons for exemption\n(3) The annual report prepared by the Director-General and given to\nthe Minister under section 46 of the Public Governance,\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013 for a period must, for\nany advice that was not published, or was published in modified\nform, under section 21 because of this section during the period,\n\n\nThe Australian Centre for Disease Control  Part 2\nPublication of public health advice  Division 5\nSection 23\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\ninclude the reasons why the advice was not published, or was\npublished in modified form.\n(4) For the purposes of subsection (3), it is sufficient for the annual\nreport to specify the subparagraph or subparagraphs of\nparagraph (a) or (b) of the definition of exempt material in\nsection 5 of this Act that applied to the advice, or that paragraph (c)\nof that definition applied."
    },
