      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "requires",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Requires specification of subparagraphs",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-23",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23 Rules may make provision about publication of public health",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-23"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.31",
      "values:originalText": "advice\n(1) The rules may make provision in relation to the publication of\nadvice under section 21.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), rules made for the purposes of that\nsubsection may do any of the following:\n(a) provide that advice may only be published under section 21\nafter the end of a specified period after the advice was given\n(which must not be longer than the 30-day period mentioned\nin subsection 21(1));\n(b) require the Director-General to inform a recipient of advice\nthat the advice is proposed to be published under section 21;\n(c) provide for consultation that the Director-General must carry\nout before publishing advice under section 21;\n(d) provide for and in relation to procedures for publishing\nadvice under section 21.",
      "skos:definition": "advice\n(1) The rules may make provision in relation to the publication of\nadvice under section 21.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), rules made for the purposes of that\nsubsection may do any of the following:\n(a) provide that advice may only be published under section 21\nafter the end of a specified period after the advice was given\n(which must not be longer than the 30-day period mentioned\nin subsection 21(1));\n(b) require the Director-General to inform a recipient of advice\nthat the advice is proposed to be published under section 21;\n(c) provide for consultation that the Director-General must carry\nout before publishing advice under section 21;\n(d) provide for and in relation to procedures for publishing\nadvice under section 21.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-23-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-23-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "02c97447687b4871b00afe98075a37426dda6be15030c7222033c471491e69f5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-23",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23 Rules may make provision about publication of public health",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 31,
      "values:originalText": "advice\n(1) The rules may make provision in relation to the publication of\nadvice under section 21.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), rules made for the purposes of that\nsubsection may do any of the following:\n(a) provide that advice may only be published under section 21\nafter the end of a specified period after the advice was given\n(which must not be longer than the 30-day period mentioned\nin subsection 21(1));\n(b) require the Director-General to inform a recipient of advice\nthat the advice is proposed to be published under section 21;\n(c) provide for consultation that the Director-General must carry\nout before publishing advice under section 21;\n(d) provide for and in relation to procedures for publishing\nadvice under section 21."
    },
    {
