    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-24",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24 Register of public health agreements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-24"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General must cause a register of public health\nagreements to be published on the Centre’s website.\n(2) A public health agreement is a written agreement between the\nCentre and one or more other entities, at least one of which is not\nan Australian government entity, under which the Centre receives\ninformation or advice in relation to public health matters.\n(3) The rules may prescribe other kinds of arrangements involving the\nCentre that are public health agreements.\n(4) The register must include the name of each party to a public health\nagreement.\n(5) Without limiting the information that may be included in the\nregister, the register may include:\n(a) information about the expertise of a party to a public health\nagreement; and\n(b) the reason for entering into a public health agreement.\n\n\nThe Advisory Council of the Australian Centre for Disease Control  Part 3\nIntroduction  Division 1\nSection 25\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Director-General must cause a register of public health\nagreements to be published on the Centre’s website.\n(2) A public health agreement is a written agreement between the\nCentre and one or more other entities, at least one of which is not\nan Australian government entity, under which the Centre receives\ninformation or advice in relation to public health matters.\n(3) The rules may prescribe other kinds of arrangements involving the\nCentre that are public health agreements.\n(4) The register must include the name of each party to a public health\nagreement.\n(5) Without limiting the information that may be included in the\nregister, the register may include:\n(a) information about the expertise of a party to a public health\nagreement; and\n(b) the reason for entering into a public health agreement.\n\n\nThe Advisory Council of the Australian Centre for Disease Control  Part 3\nIntroduction  Division 1\nSection 25\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-24-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-24-ss-2"
