    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-30",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30 Appointment of Advisory Council members",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-30"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.35",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Each Advisory Council member (other than the Director-General\nand the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer) is to be appointed\nby the Minister by written instrument, on a part-time basis.\nNote:\nAn appointed member may be reappointed: see section 33AA of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901.\n(2) An appointed member holds office for the period specified in the\ninstrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 3 years.\n(3) The Minister must ensure that at least one appointed member is an\nAboriginal person or a Torres Strait Islander (or both) who has\nexpertise, qualifications or experience in the health needs of\nAboriginal persons or Torres Strait Islanders (or both).\n(3A) The Minister must ensure that at least one appointed member is a\nperson with a disability who has expertise, qualifications or\nexperience in the health needs of people with disability.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Each Advisory Council member (other than the Director-General\nand the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer) is to be appointed\nby the Minister by written instrument, on a part-time basis.\nNote:\nAn appointed member may be reappointed: see section 33AA of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901.\n(2) An appointed member holds office for the period specified in the\ninstrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 3 years.\n(3) The Minister must ensure that at least one appointed member is an\nAboriginal person or a Torres Strait Islander (or both) who has\nexpertise, qualifications or experience in the health needs of\nAboriginal persons or Torres Strait Islanders (or both).\n(3A) The Minister must ensure that at least one appointed member is a\nperson with a disability who has expertise, qualifications or\nexperience in the health needs of people with disability.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-30-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-30-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-30-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-30-ss-3a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ade9a3c7990963de463627e5735d26c6fdd183e6e926c0373d9ec527f5298a78"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-30",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "30 Appointment of Advisory Council members",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 35,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Each Advisory Council member (other than the Director-General\nand the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer) is to be appointed\nby the Minister by written instrument, on a part-time basis.\nNote:\nAn appointed member may be reappointed: see section 33AA of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901.\n(2) An appointed member holds office for the period specified in the\ninstrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 3 years.\n(3) The Minister must ensure that at least one appointed member is an\nAboriginal person or a Torres Strait Islander (or both) who has\nexpertise, qualifications or experience in the health needs of\nAboriginal persons or Torres Strait Islanders (or both).\n(3A) The Minister must ensure that at least one appointed member is a\nperson with a disability who has expertise, qualifications or\nexperience in the health needs of people with disability."
    },
