    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-38",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "38 Meetings of the Advisory Council",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-38"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.40",
      "values:originalText": "Holding meetings\n(1) The Chair of the Advisory Council:\n(a) must convene at least 2 meetings each calendar year; and\n(b) may convene such other meetings as are necessary for the\nefficient performance of the Advisory Council’s functions.\nProcedure of meetings\n(2) Subject to this section, the Chair may, in writing, determine\nmatters relating to the operation of the Advisory Council.\n(3) Subject to this section, if no determination is in force under\nsubsection (2) the Advisory Council may operate in the way it\ndetermines.\n(4) The Chair must ensure that minutes of meetings are kept.\nMeeting to be held in private\n(5) Subject to subsection (6), meetings are to be held in private.\nAttendance by others\n(6) The Chair may invite a person to attend a meeting for the purpose\nof advising or informing the Advisory Council on any matter.\nPublication of summary\n(7) As soon as practicable after a meeting, the Director-General must\ncause to be published on the Centre’s website a summary of any\nadvice, or recommendations, relating to public health matters that\nthe Advisory Council adopted during the meeting.\n(8) The Director-General must take reasonable steps to ensure that the\nsummary does not include exempt material.\n\n\nThe Advisory Council of the Australian Centre for Disease Control  Part 3\nOperation of the Advisory Council  Division 5\nSection 38\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\nDetermination not a legislative instrument.\n(9) A determination made under subsection (2) is not a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "skos:definition": "Holding meetings\n(1) The Chair of the Advisory Council:\n(a) must convene at least 2 meetings each calendar year; and\n(b) may convene such other meetings as are necessary for the\nefficient performance of the Advisory Council’s functions.\nProcedure of meetings\n(2) Subject to this section, the Chair may, in writing, determine\nmatters relating to the operation of the Advisory Council.\n(3) Subject to this section, if no determination is in force under\nsubsection (2) the Advisory Council may operate in the way it\ndetermines.\n(4) The Chair must ensure that minutes of meetings are kept.\nMeeting to be held in private\n(5) Subject to subsection (6), meetings are to be held in private.\nAttendance by others\n(6) The Chair may invite a person to attend a meeting for the purpose\nof advising or informing the Advisory Council on any matter.\nPublication of summary\n(7) As soon as practicable after a meeting, the Director-General must\ncause to be published on the Centre’s website a summary of any\nadvice, or recommendations, relating to public health matters that\nthe Advisory Council adopted during the meeting.\n(8) The Director-General must take reasonable steps to ensure that the\nsummary does not include exempt material.\n\n\nThe Advisory Council of the Australian Centre for Disease Control  Part 3\nOperation of the Advisory Council  Division 5\nSection 38\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\nDetermination not a legislative instrument.\n(9) A determination made under subsection (2) is not a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-38-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-38-ss-2"
