    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-53",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53 Authorisation—disclosure in the public interest",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-53"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.52",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General may disclose relevant information.\n(2) However, the Director-General may only disclose protected\ninformation under subsection (1) if the Director-General certifies\nthat:\n(a) it is in the public interest to do so; and\n(b) the purpose of the disclosure could not be achieved without\ndisclosing the protected information.\n(3) If a certificate under subsection (2) is made or given in writing, the\ncertificate is not a legislative instrument.\n\n\nInformation  Part 4\nAuthorised collection, use and disclosure of relevant information  Division 3\nSection 54\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\nRules may prescribe guidelines for certificates\n(4) The rules may prescribe guidelines for the exercise of the\nDirector-General’s power to give certificates under subsection (2).\n(5) In deciding whether to give a certificate under subsection (2), the\nDirector-General must act in accordance with guidelines (if any)\nprescribed for the purposes of subsection (4).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Director-General may disclose relevant information.\n(2) However, the Director-General may only disclose protected\ninformation under subsection (1) if the Director-General certifies\nthat:\n(a) it is in the public interest to do so; and\n(b) the purpose of the disclosure could not be achieved without\ndisclosing the protected information.\n(3) If a certificate under subsection (2) is made or given in writing, the\ncertificate is not a legislative instrument.\n\n\nInformation  Part 4\nAuthorised collection, use and disclosure of relevant information  Division 3\nSection 54\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\nRules may prescribe guidelines for certificates\n(4) The rules may prescribe guidelines for the exercise of the\nDirector-General’s power to give certificates under subsection (2).\n(5) In deciding whether to give a certificate under subsection (2), the\nDirector-General must act in accordance with guidelines (if any)\nprescribed for the purposes of subsection (4).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-53-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-53-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-53-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-53-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-53-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "652d2bc32d29406b64db08a42db14130a2d313874b48925b136d0747914c0466"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-53",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53 Authorisation—disclosure in the public interest",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 52,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General may disclose relevant information.\n(2) However, the Director-General may only disclose protected\ninformation under subsection (1) if the Director-General certifies\nthat:\n(a) it is in the public interest to do so; and\n(b) the purpose of the disclosure could not be achieved without\ndisclosing the protected information.\n(3) If a certificate under subsection (2) is made or given in writing, the\ncertificate is not a legislative instrument.\n\n\nInformation  Part 4\nAuthorised collection, use and disclosure of relevant information  Division 3\nSection 54\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\nRules may prescribe guidelines for certificates\n(4) The rules may prescribe guidelines for the exercise of the\nDirector-General’s power to give certificates under subsection (2).\n(5) In deciding whether to give a certificate under subsection (2), the\nDirector-General must act in accordance with guidelines (if any)\nprescribed for the purposes of subsection (4)."
    },
