    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-56",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56 Authorisation—disclosure to oversight or integrity agency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-56"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.54",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General may disclose relevant information if:\n(a) the disclosure is to any of the following:\n(i) the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security, or a\nperson covered by subsection 32(1) of the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act\n1986;\n(ii) the Commonwealth Ombudsman, or another officer\nwithin the meaning of subsection 35(1) of the\nOmbudsman Act 1976;\n(iii) the Australian Information Commissioner, a member of\nthe staff of the Office of the Australian Information\nCommissioner, or a consultant engaged under the\nAustralian Information Commissioner Act 2010;\n\n\nInformation  Part 4\nAuthorised collection, use and disclosure of relevant information  Division 3\nSection 57\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\n(iv) the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner or another\nstaff member of the NACC (within the meaning of the\nNational Anti-Corruption Commission Act 2022);\n(v) the Inspector of the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission or a person assisting the Inspector (within\nthe meaning of the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission Act 2022); and\n(b) the disclosure is for the purpose of that person performing a\nfunction or duty or exercising a power.\n(2) To avoid doubt, this section does not limit any provision of an Act\nmentioned in subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Director-General may disclose relevant information if:\n(a) the disclosure is to any of the following:\n(i) the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security, or a\nperson covered by subsection 32(1) of the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act\n1986;\n(ii) the Commonwealth Ombudsman, or another officer\nwithin the meaning of subsection 35(1) of the\nOmbudsman Act 1976;\n(iii) the Australian Information Commissioner, a member of\nthe staff of the Office of the Australian Information\nCommissioner, or a consultant engaged under the\nAustralian Information Commissioner Act 2010;\n\n\nInformation  Part 4\nAuthorised collection, use and disclosure of relevant information  Division 3\nSection 57\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\n(iv) the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner or another\nstaff member of the NACC (within the meaning of the\nNational Anti-Corruption Commission Act 2022);\n(v) the Inspector of the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission or a person assisting the Inspector (within\nthe meaning of the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission Act 2022); and\n(b) the disclosure is for the purpose of that person performing a\nfunction or duty or exercising a power.\n(2) To avoid doubt, this section does not limit any provision of an Act\nmentioned in subsection (1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-56-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-56-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ed92debefceeba1168167e95a69a9e2724af6e508ea9a610b6e5c9f0548f4574"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-56",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56 Authorisation—disclosure to oversight or integrity agency",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 54,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General may disclose relevant information if:\n(a) the disclosure is to any of the following:\n(i) the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security, or a\nperson covered by subsection 32(1) of the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act\n1986;\n(ii) the Commonwealth Ombudsman, or another officer\nwithin the meaning of subsection 35(1) of the\nOmbudsman Act 1976;\n(iii) the Australian Information Commissioner, a member of\nthe staff of the Office of the Australian Information\nCommissioner, or a consultant engaged under the\nAustralian Information Commissioner Act 2010;\n\n\nInformation  Part 4\nAuthorised collection, use and disclosure of relevant information  Division 3\nSection 57\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\n(iv) the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner or another\nstaff member of the NACC (within the meaning of the\nNational Anti-Corruption Commission Act 2022);\n(v) the Inspector of the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission or a person assisting the Inspector (within\nthe meaning of the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission Act 2022); and\n(b) the disclosure is for the purpose of that person performing a\nfunction or duty or exercising a power.\n(2) To avoid doubt, this section does not limit any provision of an Act\nmentioned in subsection (1)."
    },
