    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-65",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "65 Authorisation—disclosure to prescribed public health entities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-65"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.56",
      "values:originalText": "Disclosure by Director-General\n(1) The Director-General may disclose relevant information to a\nprescribed public health entity for the purpose of assisting the\nentity to carry out a prescribed public health activity, if the\nconditions in subsections (4) and (5) are satisfied.\n\n\nInformation  Part 4\nAuthorised collection, use and disclosure of relevant information  Division 3\nSection 65\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\nDisclosure by designated data service provider\n(2) A designated data service provider may disclose relevant\ninformation to a prescribed public health entity for the purpose of\nassisting the entity to carry out a prescribed public health activity,\nif the Director-General has, in writing, approved the disclosure.\n(3) The Director-General may approve a disclosure for the purposes of\nsubsection (2) only if the conditions in subsections (4) and (5) are\nsatisfied.\nConditions\n(4) The condition in this subsection is satisfied if the prescribed public\nhealth entity has given the Director-General an undertaking, in\nwriting, to use or disclose the relevant information only where the\nuse or disclosure is either:\n(a) all of the following;\n(i) in accordance with the undertaking;\n(ii) in accordance with any principles determined under\nsubsection (6);\n(iii) reasonably necessary to carry out a prescribed public\nhealth activity specified in the undertaking; or\n(b) otherwise authorised by this Part.\n(5) The condition in this subsection is satisfied if the Director-General\nis satisfied that either:\n(a) the relevant information to be disclosed does not include any\nprotected information; or\n(b) only the minimum amount of protected information\nnecessary to assist the entity to carry out a prescribed public\nhealth activity is disclosed.\nPrinciples for use or disclosure by prescribed public health entity\n(6) The Director-General may, by legislative instrument, determine\nprinciples for the purposes of subparagraph (4)(a)(ii).",
      "skos:definition": "Disclosure by Director-General\n(1) The Director-General may disclose relevant information to a\nprescribed public health entity for the purpose of assisting the\nentity to carry out a prescribed public health activity, if the\nconditions in subsections (4) and (5) are satisfied.\n\n\nInformation  Part 4\nAuthorised collection, use and disclosure of relevant information  Division 3\nSection 65\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\nDisclosure by designated data service provider\n(2) A designated data service provider may disclose relevant\ninformation to a prescribed public health entity for the purpose of\nassisting the entity to carry out a prescribed public health activity,\nif the Director-General has, in writing, approved the disclosure.\n(3) The Director-General may approve a disclosure for the purposes of\nsubsection (2) only if the conditions in subsections (4) and (5) are\nsatisfied.\nConditions\n(4) The condition in this subsection is satisfied if the prescribed public\nhealth entity has given the Director-General an undertaking, in\nwriting, to use or disclose the relevant information only where the\nuse or disclosure is either:\n(a) all of the following;\n(i) in accordance with the undertaking;\n(ii) in accordance with any principles determined under\nsubsection (6);\n(iii) reasonably necessary to carry out a prescribed public\nhealth activity specified in the undertaking; or\n(b) otherwise authorised by this Part.\n(5) The condition in this subsection is satisfied if the Director-General\nis satisfied that either:\n(a) the relevant information to be disclosed does not include any\nprotected information; or\n(b) only the minimum amount of protected information\nnecessary to assist the entity to carry out a prescribed public\nhealth activity is disclosed.\nPrinciples for use or disclosure by prescribed public health entity\n(6) The Director-General may, by legislative instrument, determine\nprinciples for the purposes of subparagraph (4)(a)(ii).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-65-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-65-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-65-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-65-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-65-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-65-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "182eb5ea67fc3c2132e9d9b47a293e77a70b2c37e1fb8104e4c90a9e7deeb4b8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-65",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "65 Authorisation—disclosure to prescribed public health entities",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 56,
      "values:originalText": "Disclosure by Director-General\n(1) The Director-General may disclose relevant information to a\nprescribed public health entity for the purpose of assisting the\nentity to carry out a prescribed public health activity, if the\nconditions in subsections (4) and (5) are satisfied.\n\n\nInformation  Part 4\nAuthorised collection, use and disclosure of relevant information  Division 3\nSection 65\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\nDisclosure by designated data service provider\n(2) A designated data service provider may disclose relevant\ninformation to a prescribed public health entity for the purpose of\nassisting the entity to carry out a prescribed public health activity,\nif the Director-General has, in writing, approved the disclosure.\n(3) The Director-General may approve a disclosure for the purposes of\nsubsection (2) only if the conditions in subsections (4) and (5) are\nsatisfied.\nConditions\n(4) The condition in this subsection is satisfied if the prescribed public\nhealth entity has given the Director-General an undertaking, in\nwriting, to use or disclose the relevant information only where the\nuse or disclosure is either:\n(a) all of the following;\n(i) in accordance with the undertaking;\n(ii) in accordance with any principles determined under\nsubsection (6);\n(iii) reasonably necessary to carry out a prescribed public\nhealth activity specified in the undertaking; or\n(b) otherwise authorised by this Part.\n(5) The condition in this subsection is satisfied if the Director-General\nis satisfied that either:\n(a) the relevant information to be disclosed does not include any\nprotected information; or\n(b) only the minimum amount of protected information\nnecessary to assist the entity to carry out a prescribed public\nhealth activity is disclosed.\nPrinciples for use or disclosure by prescribed public health entity\n(6) The Director-General may, by legislative instrument, determine\nprinciples for the purposes of subparagraph (4)(a)(ii)."
    },
