    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-70",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "70 Authorisations have effect despite any other law",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-70"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.60",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A provision of this Division that authorises the collection, use or\ndisclosure of information (an authorisation provision) has effect\ndespite:\n(a) any other written law of the Commonwealth or a State or\nTerritory, whether enacted before or after the commencement\nof this Act; and\n(b) any unwritten law of the Commonwealth or a State or\nTerritory.\n(2) Despite subsection (1), an authorisation provision is subject to the\ndesignated secrecy laws.\n(3) To avoid doubt, subsection (1) does not prevent the Privacy Act\n1988 applying to the information mentioned in that subsection.\n\n\nInformation  Part 4\nAuthorised collection, use and disclosure of relevant information  Division 3\nSection 70\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\nNote:\nAn authorisation provision constitutes an authorisation for the\npurposes of the Privacy Act 1988, but personal information to which\nan authorisation provision applies is otherwise subject to that Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A provision of this Division that authorises the collection, use or\ndisclosure of information (an authorisation provision) has effect\ndespite:\n(a) any other written law of the Commonwealth or a State or\nTerritory, whether enacted before or after the commencement\nof this Act; and\n(b) any unwritten law of the Commonwealth or a State or\nTerritory.\n(2) Despite subsection (1), an authorisation provision is subject to the\ndesignated secrecy laws.\n(3) To avoid doubt, subsection (1) does not prevent the Privacy Act\n1988 applying to the information mentioned in that subsection.\n\n\nInformation  Part 4\nAuthorised collection, use and disclosure of relevant information  Division 3\nSection 70\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\nNote:\nAn authorisation provision constitutes an authorisation for the\npurposes of the Privacy Act 1988, but personal information to which\nan authorisation provision applies is otherwise subject to that Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-70-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-70-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-70-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "99e228112b77ba342a18795cf14aa90ab58d8318ba0ccbf7210083e14a968b54"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-70",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "70 Authorisations have effect despite any other law",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 60,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A provision of this Division that authorises the collection, use or\ndisclosure of information (an authorisation provision) has effect\ndespite:\n(a) any other written law of the Commonwealth or a State or\nTerritory, whether enacted before or after the commencement\nof this Act; and\n(b) any unwritten law of the Commonwealth or a State or\nTerritory.\n(2) Despite subsection (1), an authorisation provision is subject to the\ndesignated secrecy laws.\n(3) To avoid doubt, subsection (1) does not prevent the Privacy Act\n1988 applying to the information mentioned in that subsection.\n\n\nInformation  Part 4\nAuthorised collection, use and disclosure of relevant information  Division 3\nSection 70\nNo. 61, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025\nNote:\nAn authorisation provision constitutes an authorisation for the\npurposes of the Privacy Act 1988, but personal information to which\nan authorisation provision applies is otherwise subject to that Act."
    },
