    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-72",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "72 Compensation for acquisition of property",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-72"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.65",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the operation of this Part would result in an acquisition of\nproperty (within the meaning of paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution) from a person otherwise than on just terms (within\nthe meaning of that paragraph), the Commonwealth is liable to pay\na reasonable amount of compensation to the person.\n(2) If the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount\nof the compensation, the person may institute proceedings in the\nFederal Court of Australia or the Supreme Court of a State or\nTerritory for the recovery from the Commonwealth of such\nreasonable amount of compensation as the court determines.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the operation of this Part would result in an acquisition of\nproperty (within the meaning of paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution) from a person otherwise than on just terms (within\nthe meaning of that paragraph), the Commonwealth is liable to pay\na reasonable amount of compensation to the person.\n(2) If the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount\nof the compensation, the person may institute proceedings in the\nFederal Court of Australia or the Supreme Court of a State or\nTerritory for the recovery from the Commonwealth of such\nreasonable amount of compensation as the court determines.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-72-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-72-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "040c281d6a4f6177380d72acfbd63c218d4aaccb705b05cfd0042ec89edcbd09"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-72",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "72 Compensation for acquisition of property",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 65,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the operation of this Part would result in an acquisition of\nproperty (within the meaning of paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution) from a person otherwise than on just terms (within\nthe meaning of that paragraph), the Commonwealth is liable to pay\na reasonable amount of compensation to the person.\n(2) If the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount\nof the compensation, the person may institute proceedings in the\nFederal Court of Australia or the Supreme Court of a State or\nTerritory for the recovery from the Commonwealth of such\nreasonable amount of compensation as the court determines."
    },
