    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-76",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "76 Delegation by the Director-General",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-76"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.69",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General may, in writing, delegate to an SES\nemployee, or acting SES employee, in the Centre all or any of the\nDirector-General’s functions, duties or powers under:\n(a) this Act; or\n(b) Part 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act in relation to the civil\npenalty provisions of this Act.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\nException\n(2) However, the Director-General must not delegate the\nDirector-General’s functions, duties or powers under:\n(a) section 45 (direction to give information); or\n(b) section 67 (data sharing declarations).\nDirections to delegate\n(3) A person performing functions or duties or exercising powers\nunder a delegation under subsection (1) must comply with any\nwritten directions of the Director-General under subsection (4).\n(4) The Director-General may, in writing, give directions for the\npurposes of subsection (3).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Director-General may, in writing, delegate to an SES\nemployee, or acting SES employee, in the Centre all or any of the\nDirector-General’s functions, duties or powers under:\n(a) this Act; or\n(b) Part 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act in relation to the civil\npenalty provisions of this Act.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\nException\n(2) However, the Director-General must not delegate the\nDirector-General’s functions, duties or powers under:\n(a) section 45 (direction to give information); or\n(b) section 67 (data sharing declarations).\nDirections to delegate\n(3) A person performing functions or duties or exercising powers\nunder a delegation under subsection (1) must comply with any\nwritten directions of the Director-General under subsection (4).\n(4) The Director-General may, in writing, give directions for the\npurposes of subsection (3).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-76-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-76-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-76-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-76-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f547e76ac6850d4c9da9e3a5e2d21222c2c3ff45475f9c70a7845c1b031df15f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-76",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "76 Delegation by the Director-General",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 69,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General may, in writing, delegate to an SES\nemployee, or acting SES employee, in the Centre all or any of the\nDirector-General’s functions, duties or powers under:\n(a) this Act; or\n(b) Part 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act in relation to the civil\npenalty provisions of this Act.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\nException\n(2) However, the Director-General must not delegate the\nDirector-General’s functions, duties or powers under:\n(a) section 45 (direction to give information); or\n(b) section 67 (data sharing declarations).\nDirections to delegate\n(3) A person performing functions or duties or exercising powers\nunder a delegation under subsection (1) must comply with any\nwritten directions of the Director-General under subsection (4).\n(4) The Director-General may, in writing, give directions for the\npurposes of subsection (3)."
    },
