    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-77",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "77 Protection from liability etc.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-77"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.70",
      "values:originalText": "Authorised collection, use or disclosure not an offence under other\nlaws\n(1) Subject to subsection (2), a person does not commit an offence,\nand is not liable to any penalty, under any other enactment of the\nCommonwealth, or any enactment of a State or Territory, as a\nresult of the person collecting, using or disclosing information in\naccordance with this Act.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to a designated secrecy\nlaw.\nAuthorised collection, use or disclosure does not result in liability\nfor civil proceedings\n(3) A person is not liable to civil proceedings for loss, damage or\ninjury of any kind suffered by another person as a result of the\nperson collecting, using or disclosing information in accordance\nwith this Act.\nAuthorised collection, use or disclosure does not contravene\nmedical or other professional standards\n(4) A person does not contravene medical standards, or any other\nrelevant professional standards, as a result of the person collecting,\nusing or disclosing information in accordance with this Act.",
      "skos:definition": "Authorised collection, use or disclosure not an offence under other\nlaws\n(1) Subject to subsection (2), a person does not commit an offence,\nand is not liable to any penalty, under any other enactment of the\nCommonwealth, or any enactment of a State or Territory, as a\nresult of the person collecting, using or disclosing information in\naccordance with this Act.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to a designated secrecy\nlaw.\nAuthorised collection, use or disclosure does not result in liability\nfor civil proceedings\n(3) A person is not liable to civil proceedings for loss, damage or\ninjury of any kind suffered by another person as a result of the\nperson collecting, using or disclosing information in accordance\nwith this Act.\nAuthorised collection, use or disclosure does not contravene\nmedical or other professional standards\n(4) A person does not contravene medical standards, or any other\nrelevant professional standards, as a result of the person collecting,\nusing or disclosing information in accordance with this Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-77-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-77-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-77-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-77-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5b6c78f66c53add797a0414d44772912faa0027ed765dfd8d8f69d86bb38d13a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025#sec-77",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "77 Protection from liability etc.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 70,
      "values:originalText": "Authorised collection, use or disclosure not an offence under other\nlaws\n(1) Subject to subsection (2), a person does not commit an offence,\nand is not liable to any penalty, under any other enactment of the\nCommonwealth, or any enactment of a State or Territory, as a\nresult of the person collecting, using or disclosing information in\naccordance with this Act.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to a designated secrecy\nlaw.\nAuthorised collection, use or disclosure does not result in liability\nfor civil proceedings\n(3) A person is not liable to civil proceedings for loss, damage or\ninjury of any kind suffered by another person as a result of the\nperson collecting, using or disclosing information in accordance\nwith this Act.\nAuthorised collection, use or disclosure does not contravene\nmedical or other professional standards\n(4) A person does not contravene medical standards, or any other\nrelevant professional standards, as a result of the person collecting,\nusing or disclosing information in accordance with this Act."
    },
